      "text": "The program calls `get_memory()` without asking the simulator to record per-shot results, so Aer has no memory data to return. Adding `memory=True` to the `run` call fixes this.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\nfrom qiskit_aer import AerSimulator\n\ncirc = QuantumCircuit(2, 2)\ncirc.h(0)\ncirc.cx(0, 1)\ncirc.measure([0, 1], [0, 1])\n\nsimulator = AerSimulator()\n\n# FIX: get_memory() had no per-shot data because run() did not record memory -> added memory=True to the run call, because memory=True makes Aer store each shot's classical bit outcome so get_memory() can return them\nresult = simulator.run(circ, shots=10, memory=True).result()\nmemory = result.get_memory(circ)\nprint(memory)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
